          "slug": "shuffle",
          "name": "House shuffle",
          "aliases": ["shuffle", "brush step"],
          "difficulty": "Intermediate",
          "danceSlug": "bounce-challenge-shuffle",
          "summary": "The ball of the free foot brushes forward and back along the floor over a hop.",
          "description": "The house shuffle is a brushing step: the ball of the free foot sweeps forward and then back along the floor while the standing leg bounces or hops. It comes out of tap and jazz, and it is a building block for faster footwork and many travelling variations. Do not confuse it with the Melbourne shuffle or hardstyle shuffle, which grew out of rave scenes and use different mechanics.",
          "steps": [
