          "difficulty": "Intermediate",
          "danceSlug": "salsa-hop",
          "summary": "A rock step taken from salsa, driven by a little hop.",
          "description": "House took a lot from Latin social dance, and the salsa hop is the clearest example. The free foot rocks back or across behind the standing foot, the weight replaces forward, and a small hop on the standing leg carries you into the other side. It has a bouncy, syncopated feel and is a favourite for moving side to side while staying on the spot.",
